        "title": "Set Up the Integral",
        "text": "The parabola $f(x) = 6 - x^2$ is above $g(x) = x$ between the intersection points.\\n\\nArea = $\\int_{-3}^{2} [f(x) - g(x)] dx = \\int_{-3}^{2} [(6-x^2) - x] dx$\\n$$= \\int_{-3}^{2} (6 - x - x^2) dx$$",
